1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,800
Inspection quadrotors. Exact polynomial reference checks, and a simulated robot.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:16,700
First, replay a case from the paper's frozen benchmark. The red SDP projection intersects an obstacle. It is rejected, never flown.

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:25,700
Constructive recovery produces a feasible curve. The shape transition is illustrative. Exact arithmetic verifies the final path over every segment.

4
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:46,700
Next, a separate rest-to-rest example uses a Green mode to correct an affine guide, without solving an SDP. The model includes finite body size, four bounded rotors, motor lag, and a lateral disturbance.

5
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:57,700
The largest simulated tracking error is 2.32 centimeters. The minimum sampled body clearance is 16.03 centimeters.

6
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:03,700
Reference certificates and flight measurements are distinct. Reproducible simulation; no hardware safety claim.
